        "original_id": "6c5e9e55-c277-5567-ba22-e012bb0a2f00",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Volkswagen CrossBlue, Honda Pilot, Volkswagen Cross Coupé GTE Concept, CrossBlue Coupé\n- Companies: Volkswagen, Honda, Toyota, Ford\n- Systems: Volkswagen MQB platform\n- Places: United States, Canada, Detroit, Los Angeles\n- Events: 2015 North American International Auto Show\n- Topics: SUV competitors, concept cars, US market\n\nFacts:\n- The Honda Pilot is a mid-size crossover SUV manufactured by Honda and introduced in 2002.\n- Volkswagen presented the CrossBlue concept in Detroit in January 2013.\n- Volkswagen showed the 7-seat CrossBlue Coupé in Los Angeles in November 2013.\n- Volkswagen showed the Cross Coupé GTE at the 2015 North American International Auto Show.\n- The CrossBlue, CrossBlue Coupé, and Cross Coupé GTE together demonstrate the versatility of Volkswagen's MQB platform and are aimed at the US market.\n- In the American and Canadian markets, the Volkswagen CrossBlue targets the Toyota Highlander, Toyota 4Runner, Ford Explorer, and Honda Pilot as competitors.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
